---
import BlogPost from '../../layouts/BlogPost.astro';

const baskets = [
  { name: '4-Piece Chicken Strip Basket', href: '/items/chicken-strip-basket-4pc', price: '$9.99', cal: '1,020', per: 'about $2.50' },
  { name: '6-Piece Chicken Strip Basket', href: '/items/chicken-strip-basket-6pc', price: '$13.49', cal: '1,300', per: 'about $2.25' },
  { name: 'Honey BBQ Chicken Strip Basket (4-piece)', href: '/items/honey-bbq-chicken-strip-basket', price: '$10.49', cal: '1,140', per: 'about $2.62' },
  { name: '2-Piece Chicken Strips (2 for $5 menu)', href: '/items/2pc-chicken-strips', price: '$3.49', cal: '280 (strips only)', per: 'about $1.75' },
];

const faqs = [
  { q: 'What comes in a Dairy Queen Chicken Strip Basket?', a: 'A basket comes with chicken strips (4 or 6 pieces), fries, a slice of Texas toast and a dipping sauce. Country gravy is the classic choice.' },
  { q: 'How much is a 4-piece chicken strip basket at DQ?', a: 'A 4-piece Chicken Strip Basket typically costs about $9.99 and has about 1,020 calories with fries and toast. Prices vary by location.' },
  { q: 'Is the 6-piece basket worth it over the 4-piece?', a: 'If you are hungry or sharing, yes. You get two more strips for about $3.50 more, which brings the price per strip down a little. If you just want a normal meal, the 4-piece is enough for most people.' },
  { q: 'Are Dairy Queen chicken strips real chicken?', a: 'Yes. DQ chicken strips are made from whole pieces of chicken breast, breaded and fried, not ground and shaped like nuggets.' },
];
---
<BlogPost
  title="DQ Chicken Strip Basket Review: 4-Piece vs 6-Piece"
  description="DQ Chicken Strip Basket review: what comes in it, 4-piece vs 6-piece price and calories, the best sauces and which basket is the better deal."
  h1="Dairy Queen Chicken Strip Basket Review: 4-Piece vs 6-Piece"
  crumb="Chicken Strip Basket Review"
  eyebrow="Chicken strips at DQ"
  image="/Images/chicken-strip-basket-4pc.webp"
  imageAlt="Dairy Queen 4-piece Chicken Strip Basket with fries, Texas toast and gravy"
  datePublished="2026-05-18"
  faqs={faqs}
>
  <p class="lead"><strong>The DQ Chicken Strip Basket is one of the best meals at Dairy Queen.</strong> You get crispy strips made from whole chicken breast, fries, Texas toast and a dipping sauce, usually country gravy. The 4-piece costs about $9.99 and the 6-piece about $13.49. For most people the 4-piece is plenty; the 6-piece is better for big appetites or sharing.</p>

  <h2 id="prices">Chicken strip basket prices and calories</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="size-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Typical price</th><th>Calories</th><th>Cost per strip</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {baskets.map((b) => (
          <tr><td><strong><a href={b.href}>{b.name}</a></strong></td><td class="price-cell">{b.price}</td><td>{b.cal}</td><td>{b.per}</td></tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p style="font-size:.88rem;color:var(--color-text-muted);">Basket calories include fries and Texas toast. Cost per strip counts the whole basket price.</p>

  <h2 id="whats-good">What makes DQ’s chicken strips good</h2>
  <p>The strips are whole pieces of chicken breast, not shaped nuggets, so they pull apart like real chicken. The breading is thick and craggy, which keeps it crunchy and holds a lot of sauce. Eat them at the restaurant if you can; like any fried food, they soften in a closed bag.</p>

  <h2 id="gravy">Why everyone gets the gravy</h2>
  <p>Most chains give you a cold sauce cup. DQ serves warm, peppery country gravy, and it is the reason a lot of people order the basket. Honey mustard, ranch and BBQ are also available. If you like heat, ask for <a href="/items/flamethrower-stackburger">FlameThrower</a> sauce on the side.</p>

  <h2 id="which-size">4-piece or 6-piece?</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Get the <a href="/items/chicken-strip-basket-4pc">4-piece</a></strong> for a normal lunch or dinner. It is already about 1,020 calories with the sides.</li>
    <li><strong>Get the <a href="/items/chicken-strip-basket-6pc">6-piece</a></strong> if you are very hungry or splitting it with a child. Each strip costs a little less.</li>
    <li><strong>Want a cheaper option?</strong> The <a href="/items/2pc-chicken-strips">2-piece strips</a> are on the 2 for $5 menu at many stores, and the <a href="/items/7-meal-deal">$7 Meal Deal</a> includes 3 strips with fries, a drink and a sundae.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="sauced">Sauced baskets</h2>
  <p>The <a href="/items/honey-bbq-chicken-strip-basket">Honey BBQ basket</a> tosses the strips in a sweet, smoky sauce. It is messier but popular with kids. Some stores also offer a spicy sauced version. Sauced strips lose their crunch faster, so eat them first.</p>

  <h2 id="tips">Ordering tips</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Swap fries for <a href="/items/onion-rings">onion rings</a> or <a href="/items/cheese-curds">cheese curds</a> if your store allows it.</li>
    <li>Ask for an extra gravy cup if you are sharing. There is usually a small charge.</li>
    <li>Leftover strips reheat best in an air fryer or oven, not the microwave.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>See every chicken option on our <a href="/categories/chicken-strip-baskets">DQ chicken strip menu</a>, or compare with our <a href="/blog/best-dairy-queen-burgers-ranked">DQ burger rankings</a>.</p>
</BlogPost>
